# Overrides. Copy to .env.local only if you need one — the app is configured
# without this file. `.env` and `.env*.local` are git-ignored.
#
# The defaults live in `src/lib/public-config.ts`: the live HugFab API and the
# Supabase project the web app authenticates against. They are committed because
# all three values are already public — the website's browser bundle ships the
# same Supabase URL and anon key, and EXPO_PUBLIC_* is inlined into the JS
# bundle, which anyone can unzip out of an APK.
#
# Which is also the rule for this file: EXPO_PUBLIC_* is the only prefix Expo
# exposes to the running app, and nothing that is not already public may go in
# it. SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY bypasses RLS entirely and must never reach a
# client, in this file or anywhere else.

# Where the HugFab API lives. Default: https://hugfab.com
#
# Set this to point at a local `next dev`: your machine's LAN address, e.g.
# http://192.168.1.8:3000
#
# NEVER http://localhost:3000 — on a phone, localhost is the phone. It will
# always fail, and the failure looks like the API being down.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL=

# Supabase, for authentication only. Set both together to use a different
# project — a staging one, or a local `supabase start`. The anon key and nothing
# else, and it must be from the same project as the URL beside it.
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# EXPO_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
